{"title":"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807d636ecb3f86e712c17d898a541eb9296b101a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c061e7c758570036d975cd88fc534e34d8ab5267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79af15ecc7549604600f49baf6f88c10a4fe01a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} + \\frac{y^5-y^2}{x^2+y^5+z^2} + \\frac{z^5-z^2}{x^2+y^2+z^5} \\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first show that for any positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030a598145788988ed2ac3b0e21a3155acb09ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03ccd59d9894bfadfe98d5854a7f161926a3761b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} \\ge \\frac{x^4-x}{x^4+y^2+z^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"231\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Indeed, consider the difference:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1dd4e55a6e476191f7b2554263e3936a3cf02c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} - \\frac{x^4-x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} = \\frac{(x^5-x^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)-(x^4-x)(x^5+y^2+z^2)}{(x^5+y^2+z^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"631\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>The numerator simplifies as follows:\n</p><p>\\begin{flalign*}\n(x^5&amp;-x^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)-(x^4-x)(x^5+y^2+z^2) &amp;\\\\\n&amp;= x^5x^4+x^5(y^2+z^2)-x^2x^4-x^2(y^2+z^2)-x^4x^5-x^4(y^2+z^2)+xx^5+x(y^2+z^2) \\\\\n&amp;= x^5(y^2+z^2)-x^2(y^2+z^2)-x^4(y^2+z^2)+x(y^2+z^2) \\\\\n&amp;= (y^2+z^2)(x^5-x^4-x^2+x) \\\\\n&amp;= (y^2+z^2)x(x^4-x^3-x+1)\n\\end{flalign*}\n(but wait, check: actually, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/60720740c60f71f806b10880db948df66d3313ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5-x^4-x^2+x = x(x^4-x^3-x+1)?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"312\" height=\"21\" /> That doesn't factor nicely). \n</p><p>Alternatively, note that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46aef1b0579e2a8660e5d1dcd4c8a61f11f106f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5-x^2 = x^2(x^3-1) = x^2(x-1)(x^2+x+1), x^4-x = x(x^3-1) = x(x-1)(x^2+x+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"707\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>So then:\n</p><p>\\begin{flalign*}\n\\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} &amp;- \\frac{x^4-x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} &amp;\\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{x^2(x-1)(x^2+x+1)}{x^5+y^2+z^2} - \\frac{x(x-1)(x^2+x+1)}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\\\\n&amp;= x(x-1)(x^2+x+1)\\left(\\frac{x}{x^5+y^2+z^2} - \\frac{1}{x^4+y^2+z^2}\\right).\n\\end{flalign*}\n</p><p>Now, combine the terms inside the parentheses:\n</p><p>\\begin{flalign*}\n\\frac{x}{x^5+y^2+z^2} &amp;- \\frac{1}{x^4+y^2+z^2} &amp;\\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{x(x^4+y^2+z^2)-(x^5+y^2+z^2)}{(x^5+y^2+z^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{{x^5+x(y^2+z^2)}-(x^5+y^2+z^2)}{(x^5+y^2+z^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{(x-1)(y^2+z^2)}{(x^5+y^2+z^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)}.\n\\end{flalign*}\n</p><p>Thus, the entire difference becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78978de7b8af982fb4a7d5dad3554448a6174f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-1)(x^2+x+1)\\frac{(x-1)(y^2+z^2)}{(x^5+y^2+z^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)} = \\frac{x(x-1)^2(x^2+x+1)(y^2+z^2)}{(x^5+y^2+z^2)(x^4+y^2+z^2)} \\ge 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"695\" height=\"45\" /> \n</p><p>Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03ccd59d9894bfadfe98d5854a7f161926a3761b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} \\ge \\frac{x^4-x}{x^4+y^2+z^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"231\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, we have the analogous inequalities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c0a7013ecf089e9a9e98f59b01428e7fee4be86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> Therefore, it suffices to prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/83783b99464d43fd07d484a7850cb0ad4f9833ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^4-x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} + \\frac{y^4-y}{y^4+z^2+x^2} + \\frac{z^4-z}{z^4+x^2+y^2} \\ge 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"385\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>or equivalently,\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\frac{x^4}{x^4+y^2+z^2} + \\frac{y^4}{y^4+z^2+x^2} + \\frac{z^4}{z^4+x^2+y^2} \\ge \\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} + \\frac{y}{y^4+z^2+x^2} + \\frac{z}{z^4+x^2+y^2}.\\tag{1}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/1879bae7f0c76ddb3c250f8e210e9098641fb23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = x+y+z.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69ad397210fe86d147054da6630b5ae615365e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66d100296118860f80f4a4f2e1d8cbe1a83f965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz \\ge 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c46edcfd5351d138e2364cc6deaa39e3f9aa970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\ge 3, 3xyz \\ge 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Also, note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/381d935dc5d03e8d8ae2c2d1f2fd9ae4d2a6f762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy+yz+zx \\le \\frac{t^2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b247319e84ebc8dd8cb09d220d883d0a6b15336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2+z^2 \\ge \\frac{t^2}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Now, we estimate the right-hand side of (1). By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz inequality</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b30bf2fa7cff9ff1ddc479d728dfd4bc3c90957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2 \\le (x^4+y^2+z^2)(1+y^2+z^2),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b8fcf8d1caa3b4305b521c4154f5a6d183e020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2 = (x^2\\cdot1+y\\cdot y+z\\cdot z)^2 \\le (x^4+y^2+z^2)(1^2+y^2+z^2) = (x^4+y^2+z^2)(1+y^2+z^2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"798\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>It follows that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef75a6740a72de3d84edf3cf5ece64e4fedd5d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\le \\frac{1+y^2+z^2}{(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"253\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>and multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (which is positive) gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/214bdadf79ace93c80337ddb860dc9299f2fd842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\le \\frac{x(1+y^2+z^2)}{(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"253\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Similarly,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7fc3b7b6a607d70e2a6af70d325d3fe40f8c439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{y^4+z^2+x^2} \\le \\frac{y(1+z^2+x^2)}{(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2},\\frac{z}{z^4+x^2+y^2} \\le \\frac{z(1+x^2+y^2)}{(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"507\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Summing these, we obtain:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a6019454162de9d74a786525a801e90ee6bdb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\le \\left(\\frac{1}{(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2}\\right){\\sum x+\\sum x(y^2+z^2)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"481\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Now, note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a70275927d1001e7b6374a06d46b6927e1e731f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum x(y^2+z^2) = \\sum(xy^2+xz^2) = (xy^2+xz^2)+(yz^2+yx^2)+(zx^2+zy^2) = (x+y+z)(xy+yz+zx)-3xyz.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"886\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>Thus,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db89b0693987e08739dd1975415966b47a5ed20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\le \\frac{t+t(xy+yz+zx)-3xyz}{(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"377\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66d100296118860f80f4a4f2e1d8cbe1a83f965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz \\ge 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f7cf2ea3be40fa97ae60d91f77ef25ec2defd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3xyz \\le -3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" /> Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/381d935dc5d03e8d8ae2c2d1f2fd9ae4d2a6f762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy+yz+zx \\le \\frac{t^2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e9ef0cd44ee35561b2249688050e2b0938e0f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2+z^2 \\ge \\frac{t^2}{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"41\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2faa8409e4714c532483bf908c813d68d456442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2+y^2+z^2)^2 \\ge \\left(\\frac{t^2}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{t^4}{9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"243\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e52d9f64d9b5108ffc4c00ed289ea171aa0fa22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\le \\frac{{t+t\\left(\\frac{t^2}{3}\\right)-3}}{\\left(\\frac{t^2}{3}\\right)^2} = \\frac{t+\\left(\\frac{t^3}{3}\\right)-3}{\\left(\\frac{t^4}{9}\\right)} = \\frac{9\\left(t+\\left(\\frac{t^3}{3}\\right)-3\\right)}{t^4} = \\frac{9t+3t^3-27}{t^4} = \\frac{3t^3+9t-27}{t^4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"813\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p>We now show that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c39f60f5edb901ca723b8a4b206ae474a5feec6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3t^3+9t-27}{t^4} \\le 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>This is equivalent to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb641c113e123dad8b050f7bab2f4668629a35e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3t^3+9t-27) \\le t^4 \\Leftrightarrow t^4-3t^3-9t+27 \\ge 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Factor the left-hand side:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/5517bbc9135958da130c78947678f3b856b880d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^4-3t^3-9t+27 = (t-3)(t^3-9).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bdef97276f758c8c58a044b5dde234156443f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\ge 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bda61143c82a6376afa90ba3a8a335c92d76d95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t-3 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62e179a4374362f401bcdd80bb8849440b9c88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^3-9 \\ge 18,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> so indeed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb84d4b21794b551c87110aad4ad5656643e5bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(t-3)(t^3-9) \\ge 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" /> Hence,\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\sum\\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\le 1.\\tag{2}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Now, we estimate the left-hand side of (1). Note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16768086350691267ee3fdb7b145161bb748b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^4}{x^4+y^2+z^2} = \\frac{x^6}{x^6+x^2y^2+x^2z^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"267\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>and similarly for the other terms. So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472ced4f68d6ef88e824c648b2081283fe4a2380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\frac{x^4}{x^4+y^2+z^2} = \\sum\\frac{x^6}{x^6+x^2y^2+x^2z^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"324\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz inequality</a> (Titu's lemma), we have:\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\sum\\frac{x^6}{x^6+x^2y^2+x^2z^2} \\ge \\frac{(x^3+y^3+z^3)^2}{\\sum(x^6+x^2y^2+x^2z^2)} = \\frac{(x^3+y^3+z^3)^2}{x^6+y^6+z^6+2(x^2y^2+y^2z^2+z^2x^2)}.\\tag{3}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>We claim that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f07133ac62ca30f7fbe085e723b13cfaff5bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^3+y^3+z^3)^2 \\ge x^6+y^6+z^6+2(x^2y^2+y^2z^2+z^2x^2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"438\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Expanding the left-hand side:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0dfd62e75996f2eb85c969b4890e580b70635c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^3+y^3+z^3)^2 = x^6+y^6+z^6+2(x^3y^3+y^3z^3+z^3x^3).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"438\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the inequality is equivalent to\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\nx^3y^3+y^3z^3+z^3x^3 \\ge x^2y^2+y^2z^2+z^2x^2.\\tag{4}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3c7643a6ee6cd38b4282c0d41f894558223653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = xy, b = yz, c = zx.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89bf03abd33d97172910b19353d8945ff636dbe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = x^2y^2z^2 \\ge 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" /> and inequality (4) becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e0db6f372194385112474dfb0a0d2407cd4f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+b^3+c^3 \\ge a^2+b^2+c^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"215\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We now prove this. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM inequality\">AM-GM inequality</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c81d067c04c84a4fa1dbf222b1807342af2c770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+b^3+c^3 \\ge 3abc \\ge 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Also, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_mean_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Power mean inequality\">power mean inequality</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d211f120fc7186c89c6c0762e7d2633da3343a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a^3+b^3+c^3}{3}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\ge \\left(\\frac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{3}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"300\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>which implies\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513abecb8f6f09a63a42ab4fb78a3ae8b5066af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^3+b^3+c^3) \\ge 3\\left(\\frac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{3}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\left(\\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)^3}{3}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"464\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Squaring both sides (all positive) gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/23390750772888ebbad1b3c080e58cdb76ebc66b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^3+b^3+c^3)^2 \\ge \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)^3}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"262\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>That is,\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n(a^2+b^2+c^2)^3 \\le 3(a^3+b^3+c^3)^2.\\tag{5}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>On the other hand, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c6263a4762734121576baea87b7f0882ba27ce81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+b^3+c^3 \\ge 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc02d2a219c18670cbe9e4cf7e05edb0227f6690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(a^3+b^3+c^3)^2 \\le (a^3+b^3+c^3)^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"21\" /> \n</p><p>because\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17cbbf0a01a3f666c65f61697ac62e7bb7b46b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^3+b^3+c^3)^3 \\ge 3(a^3+b^3+c^3)^2 \\Leftrightarrow a^3+b^3+c^3 \\ge 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"421\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Combining with (5), we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/3010f8704457a66941df3a80d1e9634e1adc1b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2+b^2+c^2)^3 \\le (a^3+b^3+c^3)^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>so taking cube roots yields\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6abc787c186cda8656a93aea896603facddd1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2 \\le a^3+b^3+c^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>as desired. Therefore, from (3) we obtain\n</p><p>\\begin{equation}\n\\sum\\frac{x^4}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\ge 1.\\tag{6}\n\\end{equation}\n</p><p>Combining (2) and (6), we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d639a3ca07b72f53e4301835443ddd5a5870bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\frac{x^4}{x^4+y^2+z^2} \\ge \\sum\\frac{x}{x^4+y^2+z^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"288\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>which proves (1). Hence, the original inequality holds. \n</p><p>Equality occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f99894c74d93974e12480aa9d209c7e86df18cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Easy)\">Solution 2 (Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c1566104fc2bf659a5c495e6491df4df586251ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^5 - x^2}{x^5 + y^2 + z^2} - \\frac{x^5 - x^2}{x^3(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)} = \\frac{(x^5 - x^2)[x^3(x^2 + y^2 + z^2) - (x^5 + y^2 + z^2)]}{(x^5 + y^2 + z^2)x^3(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)}\\]\" width=\"613\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/391872e5448720ba9fe4812695300f58d279e4c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{x^2(x^3 - 1)[x^5 + x^3(y^2 + z^2) - x^5 - y^2 - z^2]}{(x^5 + y^2 + z^2)x^3(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)}\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54437184e42caec301fc404205748c0942185b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{x^2(x^3 - 1)[(x^3 - 1)(y^2 + z^2)]}{(x^5 + y^2 + z^2)x^3(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)} \\ge 0\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Then we get that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce89663fe240c2aefbd5ec3c60c8c1de09612a3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} \\ge \\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^3(x^2+y^2+z^2)}\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Summing all 3 terms we may get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a4c43ddffb94399f397051c3c01d9d29d8745b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} \\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} \\ge \\frac{x^2+y^2+z^2-\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{z}}{x^2+y^2+z^2}\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>So we need to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1ae865aed5e352a87e7f70b32f899d5e8b2699.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2+z^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Then by Rearrangement and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5e45496d5085a12bfa37d2b18b6fa0035efb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673eb9f9e339624c10797a95f5f0ade9bd578bb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2+z^2 \\geq xy+yz+xz = xyz\\left(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{z}\\right) \\geq \\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{z}\\]\" width=\"499\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f52a2b535ae45478bf9a36d67454ab00e69560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{cyc} \\frac{x^5-x^2}{x^5+y^2+z^2} \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"164\" height=\"53\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~ Ethanluyixuan2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO\" title=\"2005 IMO\">2005 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017125946\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.148 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 384/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15361/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.851      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.851      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19558:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017125946 and revision id 289893. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}